  "steps": [
    "Heat the oven to 325F and grease a 9x13 inch pan.",
    "Whisk the flour and baking powder together and set aside.",
    "Beat the butter, cream cheese and sugar until pale and very fluffy, at least 5 minutes. Add the vanilla and salt.",
    "Add the eggs one at a time, beating well after each.",
    "Add the flour mixture in three additions on low speed, mixing only until it disappears.",
    "Spread into the pan and bake 55 to 65 minutes, until a skewer comes out clean and the top is deep golden.",
    "Cool completely in the pan. Undressed it keeps 3 to 4 days airtight.",
    "To finish, spread with raspberry preserves, whip the cream with sugar and salt to soft peaks and spread over, then crush the freeze-dried raspberries over the top right before serving."
